  "id": "ct_wytchwood",
  "name": "The Wytchwood",
  "region": "the_wytchwood",
  "summary": "A dense old forest of blue-black pines leaning at wrong angles, one trail winding north through seven glades, a black creek across it.",
  "text": "The trees lean the wrong way and the moon comes down through them in thin silver shafts. The needles under you are soft and silent, and the sound of your own voice dies a few strides away. Hundreds of small things click in the branches. Somewhere ahead, something is breathing.",
